{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/245527-lunars-man-and-beast-man-and-weapon-dbt-evocations-crafting","id":245527,"title":"[Lunars] Man and Beast, Man and Weapon (DBT, Evocations, Crafting)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-31T12:05:31-07:00","id":245527,"title":"[Lunars] Man and Beast, Man and Weapon (DBT, Evocations, Crafting)","content":"The strength of the Lunar Exalted is the strength of mythic beasts. The strength of their Totem combined with their heroic human spirits. This is expressed through Deadly [Beast][man] Transformation.<br /> <br /> An artifact is not a beast, not the Totem. It is external to the Lunar, used by the Man, alien to the Beast. (<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Shut up, Saur Ops, I know it's not strictly true.)<br /> <br /> When the Man reaches for the power of the Tool, he forsakes the power of the Beast, and vice versa.<br /> <br /> <br /> But crafting Charms are Charms, not Evocations, so the Lunar needs to call on the Beast for that. How does the Beast respond, then?<br /> <br /> I see two possibilities: Either Lunar Attribute Charms never apply specifically to making things but always work in a more general fashion, or Lunar craft-related Charms may only craft the sort of things that a Beast might value.<br /> <br /> The first is hard to do, especially without making the Charm bland. A general &quot;do things faster&quot; Charm isn't very fun, and a Charm which supplements making swords and making battle-strategies might be trying to squeeze in multiple effects across two or more different subsystems.<br /> <br /> The second... Well, one might argue that the Beast values defensive structures like ant hills, bee hives and beaver dams, or traps like spider-webs. Perhaps even armor, at a stretch with hermit crabs. But does it really apply to swords or other weapons, which seem like an important competency for any Exalted with any kind of crafting power?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T11:20:13-07:00","id":246249,"title":"","content":"Lots of beasts make lots of things. Apes build nests, some parrots make drums, crow make hooks. They key I think for Lunars would be the ability to make what they need right now, out of anything, and feel absolutely no problem throwing it away the moment they are done with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T12:39:43-07:00","id":246322,"title":"","content":"I would also say that Lunars should have an equally strong grasp of the Crafts of men and tools. The Lunar's power is that he bridges man and beast. He can reach for either as his needs dictate. He can stand anywhere on the spectrum, but he can't access both ends of the spectrum at the same time. I would view DBT as the far beast end, and Evocations as the far man end. Lunars should be able to reach into either, or straddle the two sides while standing somewhere in the middle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T14:30:58-07:00","id":246364,"title":"","content":"I wonder if Lunar... not crafting so much as general creative efforts, might not be found in what they did with their Castes.<br /> <br /> I got the impression somewhere that part of the original concept of the Lost Castes was that the Lunars had tinkered with the natures of their own Essence (indeed, the only Exalted to have really done so). I don't know if that came across in even the First Edition book, but I feel it might be a thing worth exploring.<br /> <br /> Considering also points about how the Lunars of the Time of Tumult will not be Lunars that the returned Solars can recall...<br /> <br /> It might be in the nature of the Lunar to be a chaotic, struggling being, constantly trying to contain and contend with the storm of shapes and personality within themselves. Thus do they evoke the nature of Luna, who had to compete against many other possibilities, and absorb them into herself, in order to be born. Lunars have always had the easiest time doing this by dedicating themselves to certain endeavors or causes, adopting certain rituals and taboos, or entangling themselves in the lives of notable personages. The most potent of these grew to be forming Bonds with the Solar Exalted, although the others still existed as there weren't enough Solars to go around (even assuming that every Lunar would want a Mate).<br /> <br /> Time came that the Solars were destroyed, but for the entire Lunar Society to adopt the world way was not especially practical or desirable, not in the context of the new world and what their plans for dealing with it were.<br /> <br /> So instead their greatest minds worked on an alternative way to stabilise their own natures, and the fruits of their labour were the tattoos (although part of the process entailed destabilising their natural ability to form Castes).<br /> <br /> Hmm, I don't feel as though this idea conveys much in the way if supposition for an actual pattern to the method or drive for Lunars to exert their creative powers, but... maybe somebody with more of an eye for it can extrapolate such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T15:00:57-07:00","id":246371,"title":"","content":"I think I get what you are saying. What if the creative nature of Lunars doesn't show up so much in Craft, but in Occult, or Performance? Maybe the inhuman specialty of Craft was lost to the Lunars when they lost their Castes? Maybe it is buried somewhere in the Casteless or the Changing Moons? <br /> <br /> Interesting idea. I won't follow up too much on my opinions, because I don't have any beyond what I already said. I don't know Lunar crafting very well in 2E, and I have no idea what Lunars are going to be in 3E, other than not 1E or 2E Lunars. Mostly. Kinda. Some stuff will be there. Or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T15:01:51-07:00","id":246372,"title":"","content":"I could see Lunars working with tools by gifting them with the transformative strength of beasts they have. Or harmonising them so they become a conduit and catalyst for beast power.<br /> <br /> These knives? They're gifted by the Lunar to take on the form of the wings of a great bird. Or a flock of gulls. This blade? It's hungry like the wolf.<br /> <br /> Should this be part of crafting or part of evocation? Well, it depends on how much the Lunar should be able to give this power to others. Which depends more on the type of Lunar the Lunar is, than their splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T15:13:58-07:00","id":246378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/245527-lunars-man-and-beast-man-and-weapon-dbt-evocations-crafting?p=246371#post246371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I get what you are saying. What if the creative nature of Lunars doesn't show up so much in Craft, but in Occult, or Performance?</div> </div> </div> </div>{inhale}... No. I mean, if nothing else, the tattoos themselves are certainly crafted things, and I'd overall be averse to defining Lunar capabilities in terms of denying certain Abilities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe the inhuman specialty of Craft was lost to the Lunars when they lost their Castes? Maybe it is buried somewhere in the Casteless or the Changing Moons?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I'm saying about how tinkering with their Exalted Essence might provide insight into how and why they do certain creative things. About what the drive and method might be (method, in this case, incorporating the idea that there are innumerable ways to Craft).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}